# Grooveli Careers — SERVER-side environment variables (Edge Functions).
#
# This is not the same file as the `.env` in the project root, and the
# difference matters.
#
#   ../.env            is compiled into the browser bundle. Everything in it
#                      is public the moment the site is deployed, which is why
#                      only VITE_ values that are safe to publish belong there.
#
#   this file          never reaches the browser. It is uploaded to Supabase
#                      and read by the Edge Functions with `Deno.env.get`.
#
# Copy it to `supabase/.env`, fill in the real values, and upload:
#
#   cp supabase/.env.example supabase/.env
#   supabase secrets set --env-file supabase/.env --project-ref <your-ref>
#
# `supabase/.env` is git-ignored. Never commit it, and never paste a key into
# README.md or any other tracked file — this repository syncs to OneDrive, so a
# key in a tracked file leaves the machine whether or not it is committed.
#
# To see what is currently set:  supabase secrets list --project-ref <ref>

# Free News API — the ticker's headlines.    https://www.freenewsapi.io/
#
# Read by `supabase/functions/api/_shared/news.ts`, which both the `/ticker`
# endpoint and the scheduled sweep use.
#
# This CANNOT be moved to the browser as a VITE_ variable. Two reasons, and
# the second is the one that settles it:
#   1. A VITE_ value is inlined verbatim into the public bundle, so the key
#      would be readable in view-source and the free tier's daily quota would
#      be someone else's to spend.
#   2. The API sends no `Access-Control-Allow-Origin` header, so a browser
#      request to it is blocked by CORS before the key is even looked at.
#      Calling it from a server is the only way to call it at all.
FREENEWS_API_KEY=
